1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jumghur (Persian: جومقور‎) was the second son of Hulagu. Although according to some researchers, he may have been the eldest one.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Life He was born to Hulagu and his Oirat wife Guyuk Khatun[3] in 1234. He was descended from Genghis Khan on both sides: Hulagu was his (Gengis's) grandson through Tolui, and Guyuk was his granddaughter through Checheikhen. His ma
2 CONC ternal grandfather was Toralchi Güregen, one of the sons of Qutuqa Beki.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was left behind in Mongolia with Möngke when Hulagu left for Iran in 1253. Entrusted with his father's other wives' ordu,[4] he settled near Almaliq. However he soon found himself in a succession crisis between his uncles Kubla
2 CONC i and Ariq Böke in 1259 and had to support the latter.[5] Not much after Ariq's move against Alghu in 1263 and his surrender in the later year he deserted and left for Iran with host of other relatives of Hulagu - his wife Qutui K
2 CONC hatun, his brothers Taraghai, Tekshin, Teküder and others. Hearing news, Hulagu sent one of his commanders, Abatai Noyan, to accompany them. However, Jumghur fell ill and died in Samarqand en route.[5] His family reached Iran with
2 CONC out him. An angered Hulagu lashed Abatai with 60 lashes, accusing him of not taking care of Jumghur appropriately.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family : see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jumghur
