2 CONT Malikat Agha was a daughter of the Khan of Moghulistan, Khizr Khoja. Like many other Mongol princesses, she was married into the Timurid dynasty as a means of legitimising the latter's rule. Her husband was Umar Shaikh Mirza I, th
2 CONC e eldest son of Timur, while her sister, Tuman Agha, later became the wife of Timur himself. Malikat and her husband had four sons: Pir Muhammad, Iskandar, Bayqara and Ahmad. Following Umar Shaikh's death in 1394, she was subseque
2 CONC ntly remarried to his younger brother Shah Rukh, through whom she had one further son, Soyughatmish
