1 NAME Giāth ud-Din Tarkhān
2 GIVN Giāth ud-Din Tarkhān
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A prominent and influential noble during Tamerlane's reign. This title was given to him by Ghengis Khan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ḡiāṯ-al-Din Tarḵān, a ranking amir under Timur. Ḡiāṯ-al-Din, who traced his honorary title, Tarḵān, from a grant received by his ancestor, Qešleq, from Čengiz Khan (q.v.), had married two more daughters into Timur’s family 
2 CONT
2 CONT An important and influential noble during Tīmur's (Tamerlan) reign. According to family traditions, the title Tarkhān was given to the family by Genghis Khan personally.
2 CONT -
2 CONT Under the Chinggisids, Tarkhan was not a purely honorary title but referred to a personal status. This article examines the development of the Tarkhan status in late-fourteenth-century Golden Horde. Its point of departure is an im
2 CONC munity-yarlïq granted by Khan Temür-Qutluq (r.1391-1399) to a wealthy Muslim landowner that combines an ownership contract with a list of personal tax exemptions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tarkhan (Chinese: 達干; Arabic: طرخان‎; alternative spellings Tarkhaan, Tarqan, Tarchan, Tarxan or Tarcan) is an ancient Central Asian title used by various Indo-European (i.e. Iranian and Tokharian) and Altaic (i.e. Turkic and Mong
2 CONC olian) peoples, especially in the medieval era, and prominent among the successors of the Mongol Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT For further information please visit the below link:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://india.smashits.com/wikipedia/Gauhar_Shad
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gawhar_Shad
