2 CONT
2 CONT Tekina Khatun was the mother of Timur, founder of the Timurid Empire. Her husband was Amir Taraghai, a lesser emir of a Turco-Mongol Barlas Confederation.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Timurids, Tekina Khatun was a descendant of Genghis Khan.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONGOLS.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT The History of Timur written by Ali of Yezd records that “l’Emir Tragai pere de Timur” had been buried at Kesh[368].  m [TEKINA Khatun, daughter of ---] (-[1357]).  No primary source has yet been identified which names Timur’s mot
2 CONC her.  Petis de la Croix, in the Preface to his translation of the History of Timur written by Ali of Yezd, names “Tekine Catun femme legitime de l’Emir Tragai” as the mother of Timur[369].  The name does not appear in his translat
2 CONC ion of the History.  The Dominican sent to the French court in 1403 on an embassy from Timur states that Timur was “filz d’une mere de ville condicion”[370].  The Memoirs of Timur record that his mother died “when I had attained m
2 CONC y twenty-first year”[371].
