1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Menglitegin — married to Amir Tasu of Eljigin clan of Khongirad one daughter: Bulughan Khatun Khorasani — married to Ghazan
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arghun_Aqa#Family
2 CONT ===
2 CONT https://iranicaonline.org/articles/bologan-katun-the-name-of-three-of-the-royal-wives-of-the-mongol-il-khans-in-iran
2 CONT [3. Boloḡān Ḵātūn “Ḵorāsānī,” daughter of Amir Tesūy (whose mother was Menglī Tegen, the daughter of Arḡūn Āqā) was first married to Ḡāzān Khan before his accession; Rašīd-al-Dīn records her giving birth to a stillborn child near 
2 CONC Fīruzkūh in 690/early 1291, and she accompanied Ḡāzān part of the way on his second decisive advance against Bāydū in 694/1295. She gave shelter to her kinsman, a young son of Nowrūz (her maternal uncle) https://www.geni.com/peopl
2 CONC e/Amir-Nawruz-of-the-Oirats/6000000173283298141, on the fall of his family in 696/1297, and her name is linked with another less successful mediation (Rašīd-al-Dīn, ed. Jahn, 1940, pp. 31, 83, 86, 111).
2 CONT
2 CONT After Ḡāzān’s death, she became the seventh wife of Öljeytü on 8 Ḏu’l-qaʿda (or possibly Ḏu’l-ḥejja) 704/2 June (July) 1305. This third Boloḡān died on 5 Ṣafar 708/25 July 1308, perhaps in Baghdad, where she is said to have constr
2 CONC ucted a town (šahr) called after her Ḵorāsān. The endowments (waqf) of the ḵānāqāh that she built there were then entrusted to Rašīd-al-Dīn (Kāšānī, pp. 44, 82).]
