1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Amir Chupan, also known as Choban or Coban (امیر چوپان سلدوز), (d. November 1327), was a Chupanid noble of the Ilkhanate, and nominal general of the Mongol Empire. His father was named the Malek of the Mongol Suldu
2 CONC s clan. His ancestor was Chilaun (Чулуун), who was one of Chingis Khan's four great companions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chilaun (Mongolian: Чулуун) was a general in the Mongol Empire, known as one of Genghis Khan's four valiant warriors. His relatives, specifically his father Sorqan-Shira, helped young Genghis escape from captivity at the hands of 
2 CONC the Tayichiuds. His descendants include Chupan.
2 CONT
2 CONT His name "Chuluun" means "rock/rocky" in the Mongolian language.
