1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was a grandson of Baydu. After securing Shaykh Hasan's neutrality, Musa's patron Ali Padshah [https://www.geni.com/people/Ali-Padshah/6000000039302750353] went on to battle Arpa Ke'un [https://www.geni.com/peopl
2 CONC e/Arpa-KEUN-Arpa-Kaun-Ilkhan-of-the-House-of-Tolui-d-1336/6000000039300370333] on Jaghatu plains near Maragha on 29 April 1336. Arpa's army were led by 60 emirs, notably Hajji Taghay (son of Sutai, Governor of Diyar Bakr, from Oir
2 CONC ats), Uyghur commander Ögrünch, Torut (a son of Nari and relative of Narin Taghay), Ortuq-Shah (son of Alghu) and Chupan's son Sorgan Sira [https://www.geni.com/people/Sorghan-Siyurghan/6000000038602883890]. 
2 CONT However, soon some emirs, such as Mahmud b. Essen Qutlugh and Sultanshah Nikruz, defected to the side of Ali Padshah. 
2 CONT Battle was a defeat for Arpa and soon after he was captured in Sultaniya and killed.
2 CONT
