1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cité en 1380,  aux côtées du Grand Prince de Moscou Dmitri Ier Ivanovitch "Donskoy",  à la bataille victorieuse de Koulikovo Polié, contre le condottière turc Mamaï,  ( Lordwar, --"faiseur de rois" à la Horde d'Or,
2 CONC   pendant l'anarchie de 1359 à1378) .    Piotr Ignatiévitch  fut surnommé "Tchîrik",  nom turco-mongol qui signifie " Homme de Guerre ",  d'où procède le Nom de la famille Tchîrikov.
2 CONT
2 CONT This family is descended from the nephew of Khan Berkay, Da'yr~Kaydagul, who received the name of Peter after baptism.  The life of this Peter, who so pleased the Almighty Lord, is described in the Monthly Book  of Saints for June
2 CONC , 30, and there sufficiant details are given.  The great-great-grandson of the aforementioned Saint Peter, Petr Ignatievich Chirikov, served the Great Prince Dmitri Ioannovich "Donskoy" in the Guard Duty Regiment and took part in 
2 CONC the battle of Kulikovo against Khan Mamay.  The descendants of this Petr Ignatievich, The Chirikov family, in the same way served the Throne as Boyars, as Vice-Regents, as Stolniks, as Chamberlains, in the office of Okolnichii, an
2 CONC d in other distinguished positions and were granted fiefdoms.
