1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Moghadam dynasty truly begins with Ghazi Soltan.
2 CONT Amir Agha Khan = founder
2 CONT His son : Ghazi Soltan = institutionalizer
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Agha Khan Moghaddam - Ali Soltan of the Bayat tribe - Otar Soltan,Amir Agakhan sultan Muqaddam - Ghazi soltan -
2 CONT Period: Shah Safi Safavi : https://www.geni.com/people/Shah-Safi-Safavi-I/6000000008018997063
2 CONT =========
2 CONT Genealogical timeline highlighting key events and figures related to Ghazi Soltan Bayat, the leader of the Otuz Iqi and Sultan of the Moghadam clan of the Javanshir tribe.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. **Late 15th Century**:
2 CONT    - Under Shah Ismail I Safavi (r. 1501-1524), members of the Bayat tribe were relocated from Iran to Darband and Shirvan to support the new government. These settlements were named Boyat in their honor【13†source】.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. **1606**:
2 CONT    - Shah Abbas I replaces the Otuz Iqi leader with Ghazi Soltan Bayat, a servant from his princely period in Khorasan. This marks Ghazi Soltan Bayat's leadership of the Otuz Iqi and his eventual role as Sultan of the Moghadam, a 
2 CONC clan of the Javanshir tribe【8:2†source】.
2 CONT    - Shah Abbas I liberates Karabakh, further establishing Ghazi Soltan Bayat's position. At this time, Amir Agha Soltan Bayat is identified as the leader of the Moghadam, a subsidiary tribe of the Javanshir【16†source】.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. **1609**:
2 CONT    - With the help of Ghazi Soltan, Shah Abbas I orders the massacre of the Kurdish Mokris, who had the governorship of Maragheh but had refused Shah’s assistance request. Ghazi Soltan is granted the hereditary fief of Maragheh. H
2 CONC is leadership solidifies as he and his two sons, Aqa and Niyaz, increase the Moghadam tribe from 70 families to 10,000 families【8:2†source】.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. **1610-1614**:
2 CONT    - The Maragheh Qanate becomes independent of the Afshar confederation under the leadership of Ghazi Soltan Bayat【19†source】.
2 CONT    - The Moghadam tribe, originally a subsidiary of the Otuz Iqi in Karabagh, moves to Maragheh, significantly increasing their numbers and influence under Ghazi Soltan Bayat's leadership【12†source】.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. **1621-1622**:
2 CONT    - As a reward for providing 1000 soldiers, Shah Abbas I allows Agha Khan (Ghazi Soltan Bayat) to keep all taxes collected in Azerbaijan. From then on, the Moghadam tribe separates from the Javanshir and acquires Maragheh as an 
2 CONC hereditary fief. This solidifies the Bayat's independence from the Otuz Iqi and their establishment as the Moghadam【19†source】.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. **1629**:
2 CONT    - The non-Qizilbash tribes, including Agha Khan Moghadam's tribe, are recognized at the end of Shah Abbas I’s reign, with several possessing their fiefs in Azerbaijan. This further cements the Moghadam tribe's prominence in the
2 CONC  region【18†source】.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. **Late 17th to Early 18th Centuries**:
2 CONT    - Under Shah Safi and later rulers, the Moghadam tribe continues to hold significant power and territory in the Maragheh region, with leadership transitions within the tribe and among the Javanshir highlighting the continued in
2 CONC fluence and legacy of Ghazi Soltan Bayat's lineage【19†source】.
2 CONT
2 CONT This timeline encapsulates the rise of Ghazi Soltan Bayat from a servant in Khorasan to a prominent leader in Karabakh and Maragheh, along with the expansion and establishment of the Moghadam tribe as a significant power in the re
2 CONC gion under the Safavid Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT =================
2 CONT Bibliography:
2 CONT En 1606, Shah Abbas I remplace le chef des Otuz Iqi, par Ghazi Soltan Bayat [amir agha khan - Ibrahim Khalil of the Bayat tribe], un serviteur de sa période de prince au Khorasan.
2 CONT The Bayat were an indigenous Iranian tribe and Ghazi Soltan Bayat was a servant of Abbas’s prince period in Khorasan. In 1606, Shah Abbas replaced the Otuz Iqi leader by Ghazi Soltan (aka Amir Agha Khan - Ibrahim Khalil [at the ti
2 CONC me the leaders of the Otuz Iqi were called either Panah Ali of Ibrahim Khalil and one can deduct that Ghazi Soltan having become a leader of the Otuz Iqi inherited the title of Ibrahim Khalil).
2 CONT In 1609 Shah Abbas I ordered a massacre of the Kurdish Mokris who had the governorship of Maragheh and had refused the Shah’s request for help. The Mokris were massacred with the help of Ghazi Soltan. Ghazi was granted the heredit
2 CONC ary fief of Maragheh.
2 CONT Ghazi Soltan had 2 sons. Aqa and Niyaz. In 1610, when Aqa Soltan, head of the Moghadam tribe moved to Maragheh, it was decided that all the Otuz Iqi tribesmen who wanted to serve Aqa Soltan could go and a substantial portion used 
2 CONC to do so.  On the way, the Moghadam tribe grew from 70 families to 10.000 families.
2 CONT ====================================
2 CONT
2 CONT https://az.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%BCq%C9%99dd%C9%99m_eli
2 CONT
2 CONT Abdollah?
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Bayat tribe of the Afshar clan of the Azeri Confederacy of the Otuz Iqi Oghuz Turks of Karabakh Moghadam - Javanshir
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agha_Khan_Moghaddam
2 CONT Agha Khan Moghaddam[a] was a Safavid military leader and official, prominent in the late 16th and early 17th centuries. Of Turkoman origin, he was a member of the Moghaddam branch of the Otuziki/Otuzayeki tribe, who were based in 
2 CONC the Karabagh Province. When King (Shah) Abbas I (r. 1588–1629) removed Qobad Khan Mokri from his position in 1609, then governor of Marageh and a member of the Kurdish Mokri tribe, he appointed Agha Khan Moghaddam as its new gover
2 CONC nor (hakem). From then on, and decisively from 1610-1611, when the Mokri Kurds in Maragheh were massacred on the order of Abbas I, the governorship of the city was invariably held by members of the Moghaddam clan until the end of 
2 CONC the Qajar period.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT Amir Agakhan sultan Muqaddam - commander of Gizilbash, governor of the province, elbey
2 CONT https://www.wikizero.com/az/%C6%8Fmir_A%C4%9Faxan_sultan_M%C3%BCq%C9%99dd%C9%99m Amir Agakhan sultan lived in the late 16th and early 17th centuries. Otuziki province Moghaddam oymagındandır. He was born in Khanarkhi village of Ar
2 CONC azbar district . While Shah Abbas I was in Karabakh, Amir Agakhan, the head of the Otuziki province, appointed Sultan Muqaddami as the ruler of Maragha and asked him to clear it of invading Kurds. Amir Agakhan Sultan Muqaddam move
2 CONC d to Maragha with his native carving. After clearing the area of ​​Kurds, he became the ruler of Maragha, and the carving settled in the fertile lands of the province. The Shah exempted the whole carving from the taxes of the shep
2 CONC herd. Amir Agakhan sultan had a son named Huseyngulu khan https://www.geni.com/people/Mirza-Hossein-Ghouls-Khan-of-Maragheh-in-and-around-1678-Moghadam-Maraghei-khan-de-Maragheh-en-1677/6000000103156203896?through=6000000043984952
2 CONC 214. His dynasty ruled Maragha until the reign of Reza Shah Pahlavi.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT En 1606 Shah Abbas Safavi I libere le Karabakh [des Turques Ottoman]. A l'epoque, le chef de l'union des Otuz iki etait Amir Agha Khan Sultan Moghadam. Le Shah offrit de re-installer les Moghadam dans la province de Maragheh et d'
2 CONC y creer leur pays. Amir Khan agha Sultan Moghadam accepta la proposition du Shah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simultanement,(1606) Ebrahim Khan Agha Javanshir / Ali Bey Javanshir chef des Javanshir des Oymak de Sarijally, reste dans le Karabakh comme chef des Otuziki du Karabakh : [... A large part of Azarbaijan had been occupied by Ottom
2 CONC an Turks after the war 1578-1590. It was liberated after the war of 1603-1607. In 1606, Shah Abbas I restored Mohammad Khan Ziyad Ogly Qajar to the post of biglerbey of Karabakh (1585-1588 and 1606-1616). It was probably at the sa
2 CONC me time (1606-1629) that Shah Abbas I made Ibrahim Khalil Agha head of the Javanshir tribe from the Oymak and Sarijally, head of the Karabakh magal Otuziki. From that time on, head of the Javanshir clan became the hereditary head 
2 CONC of the Otuziki magal.] The Khans of Karabakh - Eldar Ismailov.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marāghe hwas given to Āqā Khān Moqaddam. The case of the Moqaddam tribe provides us with a good example of creating a new tribal unit. This was originally the subsidiary tribe of the Otūzīkī in Qarābāgh. ‘Abbās gave the rulership 
2 CONC of the tribe to Ghāzī Soltān, an old servant from ‘Abbās’ Khorāsān Prince’s period. According to Fa√lī’s description, they originally consisted of only 70 families but Ghāzī’s sons Niyāz and Āqā received great benefits from ‘Abbās
2 CONC  and increased in number to 10,000 families during his reign.30 When Āqā Soltān, head of Moqaddam moved to Marāghe, it was decided that all Otūzīkī tribesmen who wanted to serve Āqā Soltān could go and a substantial portion chose 
2 CONC to do so (according to Fa√lī they took 400,000 sheep). So these moves connected with the re-allotment of space as well as the reorganisation of tribal institutions and political balances in the provinces. In 1030–1031/1621–1622, Ā
2 CONC qā Khān received Shāh’ favor once more. Tax revenue of chūpānbeygī (tax on herds of sheep: here the number up to 500,000 per head) was presented to the tribe. Instead, they were ordered to give one soldier per 500 sheep (so in tot
2 CONC al 1,000 persons). Āqā Khān was given the robe of honor and became Āzarbāijān’s charkhchībāshī.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agha_Khan_Moghaddam
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Safavid_generals
2 CONT ====
2 CONT  Eskandar Beg listed tribal amīrs at the time of ‘Abbās’ death in 1038/1629. He referred
2 CONT the specific category of ‘non-qezelbāsh amīrs’ (az oymāqāt-e qezelbāsh nīstand va dar
2 CONT selk-e omārā‘-e ‘ezzām enteõām yāfte). Among 8 of them, 5 persons possessed their fief in
2 CONT ‘Ā§arbāijān’ namely: Āqā Khān Moqaddam, Sārū Khān Solªān Salmāsī, Kalb Re√ā Solªān
2 CONT Zanūzī, Khalīl Solªān Sīl Söpör, Nūr ol-Dīn Solªān Pāydār (Also see note 36). https://src-h.slav.hokudai.ac.jp/coe21/publish/no10_ses/09_maeda.pdf p.9
2 CONT
2 CONT ===================
2 CONT
2 CONT Les Moghadam sont une des dynasties fameuses iraniennes. Ils vivaient a Maragheh, Hashtroud, Teheran et dans la region de Chergar, pres de Zanjan. 
2 CONT Ceux des Moghadam qui vivaient a Maragheh et Hashtroud et Zanjan descendaient de la branche de Agha Khan Moghadam Javanshir [ Vakil Bey ], un des commandants d'armee de Shah Abbas II. Ceux de Teheran descendent du neveu paternel d
2 CONC e Ahmad Khan Moghadam, un des commandants dans les guerres Iran-Russie, qui etaient descendus vers Teheran sous les Qajar [ Ahmad Khan Rish Sepid].
2 CONT =====
2 CONT Ghazi Soltan/Amir Agha Soltan, himself a descendant of the Emirs of Karabagh ( ref: Anvar Chengizoglu).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ghazi Soltan who was already the leader of the Otuz Iqi and Soltan of the Moghadam tribe (ref: Anvar Chengizoglu), itself a clan of the Javanshir at the time of Shah Abbas I, was given Maragheh in 1609 as an hereditary fief by the
2 CONC  Shah, after he had helped the Shah get rid of the Kurdish Mukri. In an article, Ghazi Soltan is cited as one of the 5 emirs of Qarabagh. Also, he is said to have been close to Shah Abbas in Khorrasan while Shah Abbas I was still 
2 CONC a prince, and in this case Ghazi Soltan is said to have belonged to the Bayat tribe (ref: Anvar Chengizoglu). According to Richard Tapper there was a rumour that the leader of the Moghadam was not a Moghadam, which, in my mind, co
2 CONC rresponds to Ghazi Soltan being of the Bayat tribe (ref: Anvar Chengizoglu) and being made leader of the Moghadam tribe by Shah Abbas I.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ====
2 CONT Killed in 1612 by Mohammad Khan Zyadoglu Qajar 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ibrahim Khalil of the Bayat tribe : [https://www.wikizero.com/az/M%C3%BCq%C9%99dd%C9%99m_eli [ In 1606 , Shah Abbas I liberated Karabakh from the Ottomans. During this period, the head of the Bayat tribe was Amir Agakhan Sultan Mu
2 CONC qaddam. Shah Muqaddam's carving was offered by the country in Maragha province. Amir Agakhan sultan agreed and moved to Maragha with his carving. He was the ruler of Maragha and settled in the fertile lands of the carving province
2 CONC . The Shah exempted the whole carving from the shepherd, the scavenger, and other payments.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Amir Khan Agha Soltan, also known as Ebrahim Agha Moghadam Javanshir as of 1606 (liberation of Qarabagh by Shah Abbas II and creation of the Moghadam oke in Maragheh.
2 CONT
2 CONT خوانین مقدم در مراغه و هشترود و زنجان از نسل آقاخان مقدم جوانشیر از سرداران شاه عباس دوم بودند traduction: La dynastie des Moghadam de Maragheh, Hashtroud et Zanjan descend de Agha Khan Moghadam Javanshir, officier de Shah Abbas I
2 CONC I. Il est le ABDOLLAH dans la lignee des ascendants de Etemad Saltaneh I Haj Ali Khan Moghadam. Ne fin 16eme siecle - mort fin 17eme siecle.
2 CONT Ebrahim Sultan Budagh Sultan ogly - Hassan Ali Bey - Ebrahim Agha Javanshir -
2 CONT Khan de Maragheh en 1677 sous Shah Soleiman Safavi.
2 CONT Father of Ali Khan Bey.
2 CONT ====
2 CONT Maragha province belonged to the Muqaddim branch of the Javanshir tribe, one of the most famous provinces of Azerbaijan during the reign of Shah Abbas I. [2] The territory of that province was given to the lineage of the ancient M
2 CONC ir aga khan Soltan, who served the Safavid state comprehensively. [3] From this period, the descendants of Mir Agha khan Soltan ruled in turn in Maragha province. In the 1920s (after 1724), when a number of provinces of Azerbaijan
2 CONC , including Maragha, were occupied by Ottoman troops, those areas were under the rule of the Ottoman Teymur Pasha [4]. On the eve of Nadir Gulu khan's invasion of Azerbaijan, the chief tribe, led by Hasan Ali [note 1] Hasan Ali, r
2 CONC evolted and liberated Maragha from the Turks with the help of Nadir Shah.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Nadir Gulu khan came to Maragha, the head of the tribe (large feudal lord) Abdurrazaq Muqaddami appointed the governor of the province (1730). [5] Shortly afterwards, however, he fled with his family to Baghdad, fearing Nadi
2 CONC r Gulu Khan's betrayal. [6] The administration of Maragha province was entrusted to Hasanali bey Vakil (1737). [7] After the death of Hasanali bey Vakil (1744) his son Aliqulu khan Muqaddim replaced him on the basis of the officia
2 CONC l decree of Nadir shah. After the death of Nadir Shah, Aliqulu khan Muqaddim put an end to all dependence and declared Maraga an independent khanate and a ruler.
2 CONT https://az.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mara%C4%9Fa_xanl%C4%B1%C4%9F%C4%B1
2 CONT
2 CONT ====
2 CONT Amir Agakhan sultan lived in the late 16th and early 17th centuries. Otuziki province Moghaddam oymagındandır. He was born in Khanarkhi village of Arazbar district . While Shah Abbas I was in Karabakh, Amir Agakhan, the head of th
2 CONC e Otuziki province, appointed Sultan Muqaddami as the ruler of Maragha and asked him to clear it of invading Kurds. Amir Agakhan Sultan Muqaddam moved to Maragha with his native carving. After clearing it of the Kurds, he ruled Ma
2 CONC ragha and settled in the flowing lands of the province. The Shah exempted the whole carving from the taxes of the shepherd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amir Agakhan sultan had a son named Huseyngulu khan. His dynasty ruled Maragha until the reign of Reza Shah Pahlavi. https://www.wikizero.com/az/%C6%8Fmir_A%C4%9Faxan_sultan_M%C3%BCq%C9%99dd%C9%99m
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT De nombreuses personnes célèbres sont sorties du Muqaddam. Sous le règne de Shah Abbas I, le sultan Muqaddam Tizrov était l'un des chefs de l'armée Qizilbash qui a marché vers la Géorgie. L'un des grands seigneurs féodaux du XVIIe
2 CONC  siècle, Muhammadali Khan Bagir Khan oglu Muqaddam était un bienfaiteur et mécène des scientifiques. (https://www.wikizero.com/az/M%C3%BCq%C9%99dd%C9%99m_eli)
