2 CONC e betrothal of "[filiam] secundam Annam" and "cralem Serbiæ Stephanum Uresim, secundo eius filio Melotino", dated from the context to the early part of his reign[133].  Pachymeres records that "Michaelis despotæ filius natu minimu
2 CONC s Demetrius" married "imperatoris…filia…Anna"[134].  Ioannes Kantakouzenos records that "Michaeli duci" married "Annam sororem Andronici senioris"[135].  A synodal decision dated Nov 1278 granted dispensation for the marriage “rés
2 CONC ultant de leur sixième degré d´affinité”[136].  Her father arranged her marriage as part of the alliance between him and her future husband against Charles I King of Sicily.  Betrothed ([1267/68]) to STEFAN UROŠ MILUTIN, son of ST
