2 CONT * Faṣiḥ Aḥmad b. Jalāl-al-Din Moḥammad Ḵvāfi, Mojmal-e Faṣiḥi, ed. Maḥmud Farrok̲, 3 vols., Mashad, 1961. 
2 CONT * Majd Ḵvāfi: Rawża-ye ḵold, ed. Maḥmud Farroḵ and Ḥosayn Ḵadivjam, Tehran, 1966.
2 CONT * Ḡiāṯ-al-Din Moḥammad Kvāndamir, Tāriḵ-e ḥabib al-siar, ed. Moḥammad Dabirsiāqi, 4 vols., Tehran, 1954, III, pp. 268-69.  
2 CONT * Mir Moḥammad b. Sayyed Borhān-al-Din Ḵvāvandšāh Mirkvānd, Rawz̓at al-ṣafā, ed.‘Abbas Parwiz, 10 vols., Tehran, 1959-60. 
2 CONT * Nāṣer-al-Din Monši Kermāni, Semṭ al-ʿolā le’l-ḥażrat al-ʿolyā, ed. ʿAbbās Eqbāl, Tehran, 1949. 
2 CONT * Ḥamd-Allāh Mostawfi, Tāriḵ-e gozida, ed. ‘Abd-al-Ḥosayn Nawāʾi, Tehran, 1960. 
2 CONT * Moʿin-al-Din Naṭanzi, Montaḵab al-tawāriḵ-e moʿini, ed. Jean Aubin, Tehran, 1957.  Rašid-al-Din Fażl-Allāh, Jāmeʿ al-tawāriḵ, ed. Moḥammad Rowšan, 4 vols., Tehran, 1994. 
2 CONT * Moḥammad Šabānkāraʾi, Majmaʿ al-ansāb, ed. Mir Ḥāšem Moḥaddeṯ, Tehran, 1984.  Šehāb-al-Din (or Šaraf-al-Din) ʿAbd-Allāh Waṣṣāf-al-Ḥażra, Tajziat al-amṣār wa tazjiat al-aʿṣār (commonly referred to as Tāriḵ-e Waṣṣāf), Bomba
2 CONC y, 1853; ed. Iraj Afšār, Maḥmud Omidsālār, and Nāder Moṭallebi, Tehran, 2009. 
2 CONT * Aḥmad-ʿAli Khan Waziri Kermāni, Tāriḵ-e Kermān, ed. Moḥammad-Ebrāhim Bastāni Pārizi, 2 vols., Tehran, 1985, pp. 439-53.
2 CONT * Studies. 
2 CONT * Moḥammad-Ebrāhim Bastāni Pārizi, “Madrasa-ye torkān-e saljuqi wa torkān-e ḵatāʾi dar Kermān,” in Moḥammad-Rasul Daryāgašt, ed., Kermān dar qalamrow-e taḥqiqāt-e irāni, Kerman, 1991, pp. 55-68.
2 CONT * Širin Bayāni, Zan dar Irān-e ʿaṣr-e Moḡol, Tehran, 1973.
2 CONT * Moḥammad-Rasul Daryāgašt, ed. Kermān dar qalamrow-e taḥqiqāt-e irāni, Kerman, 1991.   
2 CONT * ʿAbbās Eqbāl, Tariḵ-e Moḡol, Tehran, 1997. 
2 CONT * Gavin R. G. Hambley, ed., Women in the Medieval Islamic World: Piety, Power and Patronage, Basingstoke, 1998. 
2 CONT * Josef Hammer-Purgstall, Geschichte der Ilchane, das ist der Mongolen in Persien 1200-1350,  2 vols., Darmstadt, 1842 (vol. I), 1843 (vol. II); repr., Amsterdam, 1974.
2 CONT * Ann K. S. Lambton, Continuity and Change in Medieval Persia: Aspects of Administrative, Economic and Social History, 11th-14th Century, London, 1988. 
2 CONT * Idem, “Awqāf in Persia 6th-8th/12th-14th Centuries: Social and Economic Aspects of Muslim waqf,” Islamic Law and Society 4/3, Leiden, 1997, pp. 298-318. 
2 CONT * Alekseĭ Konstantinovich Markov, Inventarnyĭ katalog musul’manskikh monet Imperatorskago Érmitazha (Catalogue of the Islamic coins  in the Imperial Hermitage), St. Petersburg, 1896. 
2 CONT * Moḥammad Qazvini, Yāddāšthā-ye Qazvini I, Tehran, 1953, pp. 240-46. 
