2 CONT ... During his time as ruler, Malek became increasingly violent and quickly grew unpopular with many of his subjects. This, combined with the spread of the bubonic plague in the region, prompted many citizens to leave the area. Hi
2 CONC s hated rule was finally ended when Jani Beg of the Golden Horde invaded in 1357. Malek fled, but was captured and hung in Tabriz, to the joy of the local populace. Malek's mother and children were taken by Jani Beg upon his depar
2 CONC ture from the region. His son Temürtas was killed by Hasan Buzurg's successor Shaikh Uvais in 1360, while his daughter Soltanbakt was mentioned as having been in Shiraz. Malek's death signified the end of Chobanid rule in Persia. 
2 CONT ------
2 CONT Contemporain de Jani Beg(r.1342-1347)
2 CONT
2 CONT Il succede a son frere Hassan en 1343  -1347 - rules Tabriz 1344-1358 Dernier Ilkhan des Chupanides. p 159 Kingship and Ideology of the Islamic and Mongol worlds by Anne F. Broadbridge
2 CONT
2 CONT Sanguinaire et avide - allie pour peu de temps a Abu Eshaq [ p 31 Shiraz in the Age of Hafez: The Glory of a Medieval Persian City By John Limbert]
2 CONT
2 CONT [... When Sheikh Hassan Chupani (Kuchek) was on his death bed, Malek Ashraf, his brother was directing his troops towards Fars. Upon hearing the news of his brother's death he arrived in Tabriz and apointed Anushirvan as the Ilkha
2 CONC n. But after a while, he deposed him, claiming his independance. Malek Ashraf ruled over Azarbaijan mercilessly for 14 years. any of the great scholars leaved their cities. For instance Shekh Sadr Aldin fled to Gilan.] ref p 194 I
2 CONC ranian History at a Glance http://bit.ly/1Pu8qqA
2 CONT
2 CONT Malek Ashraf (ملک اشرف), (died 1357) was a Chupanid ruler of northwestern Iran during the 14th century. He was the last of the Chupanids to possess a significant influence within Persia. He was the son of Timurtash. Malek Asraf di
2 CONC stinguished himself while serving under his brother Hasan Kucek, defeating an army of Khurasan sent by Togha Temur against Hasan in 1341. He then became embroiled in the conflict with the Injuids over Shiraz. Malek Asraf received 
2 CONC a request for assistance by the Injuid Abu Ishaq against the former's cousin Pir Hosayn, following which Malek defeated Pir Hosayn in August 1342, allowing Abu Ishaq to temporarily regain control of Shiraz. Upon the death of Hasan
2 CONC  Kucek in 1343, the Chobanid lands were at first split between Malek and his uncles Yagi Basti and Surgan. However, the division did not last, and Malek defeated Surgan in battle. After having Yagi Basti murdered, he again triumph
2 CONC ed over Surgan in 1345. Having unified the Chobanid lands, he placed a puppet (Anusirvan-i 'Adel) on the throne and ruled in his name. Malek soon became embroiled with the Jalayirids, under the rule of Hasan Buzurg. Malek sent his
2 CONC  brother, Malek Astar, to capture Baghdad in the first half of 1347, but the campaign failed with heavy losses. In 1350 he also attempted to wrest Fars from the Injuids, but failed to take Isfahan and was forced to settle for trib
2 CONC ute. During his time as ruler, Malek became increasingly violent and quickly grew unpopular with many of his subjects. This, combined with the spread of the bubonic plague in the region, prompted many citizens to leave the area. H
2 CONC is hated rule was finally ended when Jani Beg of the Golden Horde invaded in 1357. Malek fled, but was captured and hung in Tabriz, to the joy of the local populace. Malek's mother and children were taken by Jani Beg upon his depa
2 CONC rture from the region. His son Temürtas was killed by Hasan Buzurg's successor Shaikh Uvais in 1360, while his daughter Soltanbakt was mentioned as having been in Shiraz. Malek's death signified the end of Chobanid rule in Persia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Malek sent his brother, Malek Astar, to capture Baghdad in the first half of 1347, but the campaign failed with heavy losses. In 1350 he also attempted to wrest Fars from the Injuids, but failed to take Isfahan and was forced to s
2 CONC ettle for tribute.   ref. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malek_Ashraf
