1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [Hassan Ali Bey] - Agha Khan e Saani - Ghazi Soltan Moghadam
2 CONT
2 CONT Nyaz
2 CONT
2 CONT Persian sources explicitly identify Ghazi Soltan as the direct successor of Amir Agha Khan, under the name Agha Khan II, thereby confirming the establishment of a dynastic transmission of power in Maragheh. This succession, presen
2 CONC ted without any mention of conflict, suggests a rapid stabilization of Moghadam authority in the region. From this generation onward, power no longer relied solely on imperial delegation, but became rooted in a recognized heredita
2 CONC ry lineage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il represente les Moghadam a Maragheh.[Ali Khan Bey son of Ibrahim Khalil, under Shah Abbas I, was ruler of the Javanshir clan and clan of the Otuz Iqi at the end of the 16th c. with his brother Mirza Hossein.]
2 CONT
2 CONT [Ali Khan Bey son of Ibrahim Khalil, under Shah Abbas I, was ruler of the Javanshir clan and clan of the Otuz Iqi at the end of the 16th c. with his brother Mirza Hossein.]
2 CONT
2 CONT [Ghazi Soltan Moghadam] Ali Khan Bey son of Ibrahim Khalil, under Shah Abbas I, was ruler of the Javanshir Clan and clan of Otuz-Iki at the end of the 16th c. with his brother Mirza Hossein. 
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT La famille d'Ahmad Khan Moghaddam de Maragheh a reçu en fief la ville de Maragheh sous le règne du Shah Abbas II par leur ancêtre éminent, Agha Khan Moghaddam Javanshir. Après lui, son fils Ghazi Sultan (Agha Khan II) lui a succéd
2 CONC é
