2 CONT D'apres Adib ol-Molk Ghaem Magham et Mohammad Hassan Khan Etemad Saltaneh II, leur pere Haj Ali Khan Etemad Saltaneh I descend de Hossein fils de Mohammad Rassoul fils de Abdollah fils de Jafar lequel descend par 7 generations de 
2 CONC Berdi Beg fils de Oz Bek fils de Jochi fils de Chengiz Khan.
2 CONT  ادیب الملك فرزند میرزا علی خان در شرح حالی كه برای پدرش نگاشته سلسله احفاد او را چنین ذكر می كند: علی بن حسین بن محمد رسول بن عبدالله بن جعفر كه جعفر از هفت پشت واسطه به «بردی بگ بن اوزبك خان بن جوجی خان مغول» می رسد http://khaba
2 CONC rfarsi
2 CONT
2 CONT Traduction: [... Berdi Bek ben Oz Bek ben Jouji (Jochi) ben Chengiz Khan]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==========
2 CONT Muhammad Berdibek Khan (about 1310 - 1359 ) - Khan of Ulus Jochi (Golden Horde) ( 1357 - 1359 ). Janibek's son and successor .
2 CONT
2 CONT By religion - Muslim (had a Muslim name Muhammad). Under the command of Janibek he took part in the conquest campaign to Azerbaijan in 1356 . After the completion of the campaign, his father left to rule in Tabriz , but, having re
2 CONC ceived information about Janibek's illness, he returned to the Horde to take part in the struggle for power.
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to power in the summer or autumn of 1357 . According to Persian and Tatar sources, Berdibek's father, Janibek, died a natural death from a serious illness after a campaign in Persia; according to a Russian source, Berdibek
2 CONC  organized a conspiracy that led to the murder of his seriously ill father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Immediately after the ceremony of taking office, Berdibek ordered to physically destroy all representatives of the Batu Khan clan , who could be his real or potential competitors. In total, 12 of his relatives were killed, includi
2 CONC ng his 8-month-old brother (according to the Arab author Muin ad-Din Natanzi , the new khan killed him by hitting the ground).
2 CONT
2 CONT Berdibek gave the Russian Metropolitan Alexy a label (letter of gratitude) confirming the liberation of the Russian Church from tributes and extortions. In 1358 he gave a label to the Venetian ambassadors Giovanni Quirini and Fran
2 CONC cesco Bonu, confirming the right of merchants from Venice to live and trade in Azov and Provato (Dvuyakornaya bay) and allowing these merchants to trade in the Crimean ports of Kalitre, or Kaliera ( Koktebel ), and Soldaye ( Sudak
2 CONC  ).
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Arab author Ibn Khaldun, one of the highest administrative positions, beklarbek , at the court of Berdibek was occupied by Mamai .
2 CONT
2 CONT He ruled until the end of summer or early autumn of 1359 , when he was killed in a coup that brought the new Kulpu (Kulpu) Khan to power . Together with Berdibek, his closest comrade-in-arms Tughlu-bai died (in Russian chronicles 
2 CONC he was called Tovlubiy), who played a key role in his coming to power.
2 CONT
2 CONT The death of Berdibek marked the beginning of a long-term turmoil in the Horde, which the Russian chroniclers called "the great jam." In the icon of Dionysius 's workshop "Metropolitan Alexy with his life" [1], Berdibek is depicte
2 CONC d 2 years before his death, meeting in 1357 , Metropolitan Alexy , who came to the Horde [2] .
2 CONT
2 CONT Reflection in art Berdibek is one of the characters in the historical novel "The Wind of Time " by D. M. Balashov from the cycle " Sovereigns of Moscow ".
2 CONT
2 CONT ref: translation of Russian https://www.wikiwand.com/ru/%D0%91%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%BA
