2 CONT i)       '''   EIRENE Raoulaina''' ( [1265/70]- ).  Pachymeres records the marriage of "Porphyrogenito" to "[uxorem] ex Raulis stirpe"[623].  In a later passage, Pachymeres clarifies her parentage when he records that the "avia pa
2 CONC terna" of "coniux Porphyrogeniti" was "Strategopulinæ neptis ex fratre"[624].  Her birth date is estimated from her marriage in [1291].  If correct, it suggests that her father must have been one of his parents´ youngest children.
