1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_II_Doukas_of_Thessaly
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John II Doukas''', also Angelos Doukas (Latinized as ''Angelus Ducas'') (Greek: '' Ἰωάννης Ἄγγελος Δούκας '', romanized: ''Iōannēs Angelos Doukas''), was ruler of Great Vlachia (Thessaly) from 1303 to his death in 1318. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/byzant/byzant4.html
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Angelos family==
2 CONT
2 CONT One Manolis Angelos from Philadelphia  , had issue:
2 CONT *A1. Konstantinos Angelos, admiral of Sicily, *ca 1085, +after VII.1166; m.ca 1120 Theodora Komnene (*5.1.1096/97)
2 CONT **B1. Ioannes Dukas, pretender to the throne in 1199, +1200; m.two women named Zoe
2 CONT *** ...
2 CONT ***C7. [illegitimate] Michael I Komnenos Dukas, +murdered ca 1215; m.N, a dau.of N.Melissenos; 2m: 1204 N, his 1st wife's sister
2 CONT **** ...
2 CONT ****D5. [illegitimate] MICHAÉL II Komnenos Dukas Notho Angelos, Archon of Epirus and Aetolia, *1205, +1266;    m.ca 1230 Theodora Dukaina Petraliphaina
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT *****E7. [illegitimate] Ioannes Dukas Komnenos, Archon of Neaipatrai, +ca 1289; m.before 1259 a dau.of the Vlach Voivode Taronas
2 CONT ******F1. Konstantinos Komnenos Dukas, Archon of Neaipatrai, +1303; m.Anna Evagionissa (+1317)
2 CONT ******G1. '''Ioannes Dukas Angelos, Archon of Neaipatrai, +1318'''; m.1315 Eirene, illegitimate dau.of Emp Andronikos II Palaiologos
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_II_Doukas_of_Thessaly
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/THESSALONIKI.htm#IoannesDAdied1318
