2 CONT Qutb Shahi Dynasty
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Quli Qutb-ul-Mulk (Founder of Qutb Shahi dynasty, r. 1518–1543)
2 CONT Daughter 1 (e.g., Khadija Sultana, married Ibrahim Adil Shah I of Bijapur).
2 CONT Daughter 2 (e.g., Amina Begum Qutb Shahi, hypothetical, married into Mughal nobility).
2 CONT Amina Begum Qutb Shahi
2 CONT Married a Mughal officer/noble stationed in Punjab or Deccan under Emperor Akbar.
2 CONT Their offspring likely migrated to the Punjab region for administrative roles.
2 CONT Ratyal Mughal Ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT Mughal Officer in Punjab (Late 16th–17th century)
2 CONT Descendant of Amina Begum Qutb Shahi and her Mughal husband.
2 CONT Settled in Pothwar/Mirpur regions under Mughal expansion into northern Punjab.
2 CONT Rajwali of Ratyal Mughals (Late 17th–18th century)
2 CONT Prominent Mughal noble in the Ratyal clan.
2 CONT Married a woman of Qutb Shahi descent, maintaining Persian-Deccan cultural heritage.
2 CONT Family Tree Summary
