1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [Mihr Nigar Khanum was the first wife of Sultan Ahmed Mirza, the King of Samarkand and Bukhara. She was a princess of Moghulistan by birth and was the eldest daughter of Yunus Khan, the Great Khan of Moghulistan an
2 CONC d his chief consort Aisan Daulat Begum. She was also the aunt of Emperor Babur, the founder of the Mughal Empire of India as well as its first Emperor.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In July 1500, after her husband's death, she was captured by Muhammad Shaybani, the Khan of the Uzbeks; and was forcibly married to him as part of the spoils.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mihr Nigar Khanum was married to Sultan Ahmad Mirza, the eldest son and successor of Abu Sa'id Mirza,[3] as per the wishes of her father, Yunus Khan, who said: "Sultan Abu Sa'id Mirza turned the enmity that existed between Moghul 
2 CONC and Chagatai into friendship. I wish now to cement this friendship with a family alliance, and therefore offer my daughter [Mihr Nigar], as a wife, to the son of Sultan Abu Sa'id Mirza." Mihr Nigar Khanum bore her husband no child
2 CONC ren,[3] but remained in his harem for as long as he was alive, until his death in 1494.]...
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mihr_Nigar_Khanum
