1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodora_Palaiologina_Synadene
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Theodora Palaiologina Synadene''' (Greek: Θεοδώρα Παλαιολογίνα Συναδηνή) was the daughter of Constantine Palaiologos and Irene Komnene Laskarina Branaina. Through her father, she was a half-niece of the Byzantine Emperor Michae
2 CONC l VIII Palaiologos.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Early life
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Both of Theodora's parents died when she was young and unmarried, after which time she was brought up under the guardianship of her paternal half-uncle, the emperor Michael VIII.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT Sometime after being taken in by her half-uncle,[1] Theodora was married to a Byzantine noble named John Angelos Doukas Synadenos,[2] by whom she had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Euphrosyne Synadene.[3] A nun.
2 CONT *Theodore Synadenos.[4] Protostrator. Married Eudokia Muzakiaina[5] (A picture of Theodore and his wife can be seen here).
2 CONT *John Synadenos.[4] Megas Konostaulos. Married Thomais Komnene Doukaina Laskarina Kantakouzene Palaiologina.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT    Later life
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT It was not long after the death of her husband that Theodora decided to create the convent of Bebaia Elpis ("Sure Hope"[7]) in Constantinople, bringing her daughter, Euphrosyne, along with her.[8] Sometime in the 14th century, she
2 CONC  wrote the Typicon of Bebaia Elpis
2 CONT
2 CONT The exact year of Theodora's death is unknown, though it was certainly in the 14th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
