1 NOTE Michael Asen, who had gained the throne of Bulgaria when his mother had poisoned his half brother Kalman I, was himself assassinated by his cousin, Kaliman II in 1257.
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Asen, son of Ivan Asen II, came to the throne of the 2nd Kingdom of Bulgaria in 1248, after Michael's mother had poisoned his half brother Kalman I.  Michael ruled until 1257.  He was succeeded by Kaliman II.
