1 NAME Helena "Olga"
2 GIVN Helena "Olga"
1 NAME Elena ? / Olga ?
2 GIVN Elena ? / Olga ?
2 SURN
1 NAME Елена / Гелена / Ольга?
2 GIVN Елена / Гелена / Ольга?
2 SURN
1 SEX F
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1183
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Elena (?) Helena (?) Kominina''' - the second wife of Yuri Vladimirovich Dolgorukiy; nothing is reliably known about her, except that she died in 1183.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since Dolgoruky's children from this marriage were taken away by their mother during her flight to '''Byzantium''' in 1161, historian N. M. Karamzin conjectured about the Greek origin of Dolgoruky's second wife and that she belong
2 CONC ed to the royal house of Komnenos. No evidence to support Karamzin's assumptions was ever found in the sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons Mstislav and Vasilko, judging by the chronicle, were favorably received in Byzantium and received land holdings. In some sources, this princess is called "Olga". Karamzin and later researchers spoke out against the fact that 
2 CONC her name was "Elena".
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Vasilko (Vasily) (d. 1162), Prince of Suzdal.
2 CONT # Mstislav (d. 1162), Prince of Novgorod.
2 CONT # Yaroslav (d. 1166).
2 CONT # Svyatoslav (d. 1174), Prince of Yuriev.
2 CONT # Mikhail (d. 1176), Grand Duke of Vladimir-Suzdal (1174-1176).
2 CONT # Vsevolod III "the Big Nest" (1154-1212), Grand Duke of Vladimir-Suzdal (1176-1212).
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Additional sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuri_Dolgorukiy#Marriages_and_children Yuri_Dolgorukiy Marriages and children]
2 CONT
2 CONT * From [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#IuriiVladimirovichdied1158B Medlands]: She adopted the name OLGA in Russia. Her father was Isaac Komnenos (d. 1152).
2 CONT
2 CONT * From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Komnenos_(son_of_Alexios_I) Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Komnenos (son of Alexios I) was married c. 1110 to Irene, who may have been either the anonymous daughter of Volodar of Peremyshl (r. 1085–1124), known from the Slavonic Primary Chronicle to have married "the son of Emperor 
2 CONC Alexios", or, according to a different hypothesis, Kata, a daughter of David IV of Georgia (r. 1089–1125). Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Komnenos (born c. 1112), called Tzelepes (from the Turkish title Çelebi). He accompanied his father during his exile and married a daughter of Leo I, Prince of Armenia. In 1139, he defected to the Sultanate of Rum, became a
2 CONC  Muslim, settled at the Seljuk capital of Ikonion and married Sultan Mesud's daughter.
2 CONT # A daughter (born c. 1114), possibly named Maria, who married the military commander Joseph Bryennios.
2 CONT # Anna Komnene (born c. 1116), who married the courtier and ambassador John Arbantenos.
2 CONT # Andronikos I Komnenos (c. 1118 – 1185), adventurer and eventually emperor in 1183–1185.
2 CONT # In addition, Isaac had a foster son, Constantine, whom he called by the diminutive Kostintzes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT # Eudokia Komnene, who probably married Constantine Palaiologos.
2 CONT # Helena Komnene (d. 1183), who probably married Yury Dolgorukiy of Kiev.
