2 CONT       Built Moskva in 1147.
1 NOTE Grand Duke Yuri Dolgorusky died in 1157.  He was succeeded by Andrew Bogolyubsky, who did not live in Moscow, either, but remained in the north in the Grand Duchy Vladimir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yuri Dolgorusky Vladiriovich, son of Vladimir Monomakh, was entrusted by his father with the rule of the unsettled regions around the central Volga River.  Yury/Yuri founded the city of Moscow in the 1150's., and soon gained the a
2 CONC rea around the Dneiper, bringing lots of colonists to his new town.  He remained in Kiev as Grand Duke.
1 NOTE He was the founder of Moscow.
1 NOTE He was the founder of Moscow.
1 NOTE KNOWN AS "LONGHANDED"; PRINCE OF ROSTOV, SUZDAL 1094-1157; PRINCE OF
2 CONT PEREYASLAVI 1133-1135; GRAND PRINCE OF KIEV 1154-1157
