1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Olga born c.a. 1270, died c.a. 1320, was a second wife of Gediminas (Jewna / Jaune / Jauné / Ewa? / Eva? was third wife of Gediminas, and Wida / Vinda / Gvidona? was the first wife of Gediminas) - according to Gali
2 CONC tzine-family genealogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are considerable doubts about how many wives Gediminas had. Some suggest that Gediminas had two wives, one from local pagan nobles, and Jewna, an Orthodox. C. S. Rowell claims that Gediminas had only one wife, an unknown pag
2 CONC an duchess. He argues that an important marriage to a Ruthenian or Polish princess like Jewna would have been noted in contemporary sources.
