1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Matthew Asen Kantakouzenos''' or Cantacuzenus (Greek: Ματθαίος Ασάνης Καντακουζηνός, Matthaios Asanēs Kantakouzēnos, Bulgarian: Матей Асен Кантакузин, "Matey Asen Kantakuzin" c. 1325 – 15 June 1383) was Byzantin
2 CONC e Emperor from 1353 to 1357.
2 CONT
2 CONT - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Kantakouzenos
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthew Asanes Kantakouzenos was the son of Emperor John VI Kantakouzenos and Irene Asanina. In return for the support he gave to his father during his struggle with John V Palaiologos, he was given part of Thrace as an appanage i
2 CONC n 1347, and was proclaimed joint emperor in 1353, when open civil war broke out again with John V.
2 CONT
2 CONT The History of John VI Kantakouzenos records the marriage of Irene to Matthew Kantakouzenos in 1340 / early in 1341.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had at least five children:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Kantakouzenos (c. 1342 – after 1361), despotēs.
2 CONT # Demetrios I Kantakouzenos (c. 1343 – 1383), sebastokratōr. Briefly ruled the Despotate of Morea.
2 CONT # Theodora Kantakouzene. Eldest daughter. The History records her being educated by her paternal grandmother Irene Asanina, under the monastic name Eugenia. Presumed to have become a nun herself.
2 CONT # Helena Kantakouzene. Married Count Luis Fadrique of Salona, a descendant of Alfonso Fadrique. She served as Regent of Salona from 1382 to 1394.
2 CONT # Maria Kantakouzene. Married John Laskaris Kalopheros, a man of senatorial rank from the Kingdom of Cyprus.
2 CONT # (possibly) Theodore Kantakouzenos (after 1361 – 1410), ambassador to France and Venice.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicols wrote there were only TWO sons, John and Demetrios.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Nicol, Donald M. (1968). The Byzantine Family of Kantakouzenos (Cantacuzenus), ca. 1100–1460: A Genealogical and Prosopographical Study. Dumbarton Oaks studies 11. Washington, DC: Dumbarton Oaks Center for Byzantine Studies. OCL
2 CONC C 390843. [https://books.google.com/books?id=HqdBAAAAIAAJ GoogleBooks]
2 CONT *Nicol, Donald M. “The Byzantine Family of Kantakouzenos: Some Addenda and Corrigenda.” Dumbarton Oaks Papers, vol. 27, 1973, pp. 309–315. JSTOR, http://www.jstor.org/stable/1291347. Accessed 13 Mar. 2021.
