2 CONT '''John Comnenus Duke Palaeologus Synadinus''' ( Ancient Greek : Ἰωάννης Κομνηνός Δούκας Παλαιολόγος Συναδηνός ) was a Byzantine aristocrat and military leader from the early 14th century, who held the throne . [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT John is the son of the great stratopedarch John Sinadin and Theodora Paleologina . He is the brother of the protostrator Theodore Sinadine . He inherited the surname Palaeologus from his mother .
2 CONT
2 CONT He is married twice. [3] His first wife was Tomaisa Comnina Dukina Lascarina Cantacuzino Palaeologina [4] [3] , who was a descendant of the Lascarids and Palaeologans , but more precise information about her parents is missing. Fr
2 CONC om her John had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Irina Komnina Kantakuzina Paleologina Asenina , married around 1330 to Mikhail Komnin Tornik Asen Palaeologus ; [5] [3]
2 CONT *Anna Filantropina Kantakuzina Komna Paleologina Vrienisa [3]
2 CONT His second wife is Irina Laskarina Dukina Paleologina , with whom he is depicted in the Statute of the Monastery of the Holy Mother of God Safe Hope , founded by his mother Theodora. Little is known about the military-political ca
2 CONC reer of John - it is known only that he acted as an envoy of Emperor Andronicus III Palaeologus to his grandfather Andronicus II Palaeologus during the last stage of the civil war between them (1321 - 1328) . [6]
