2 CONT '''IOANNES Doukas Komnenos ([1128]-killed in battle Myriokephalon shortly after 17 Sep 1176)'''. ...  m ([1146]) --- Taronitissa, daughter of [IOANNES] Taronites [III] & his wife --- ([1125/30]-after 1176).  ... Ioannes Doukas Kom
2 CONC nenos & his wife had two children:
2 CONT *i)          MARIA Komnene (1154-before Oct 1217). ...
2 CONT *ii)         [ALEXIOS Komnenos (-1187).  Niketas Choniates records that "Comnenus Alexius, Manuel imperatoris ex fratre nepos" rebelled against Emperor Andronikos[216].  The primary source which confirms his parentage more specifi
2 CONC cally has not yet been identified, but he may have been the son of Ioannes Doukas Komnenos.  He could not have been the son of Ioannes´s brother Alexios, because of the Byzantine convention whereby sons were not normally named aft
2 CONC er their fathers, and no other son of one of the emperor´s brothers is known to have had sons.  With Norman help, he was proclaimed emperor in Thessaloniki.  Imprisoned and blinded 7 Nov 1185, he died in prison.] 
2 CONT
