1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartolomeo_Zaccaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartolomeo (or Bartolommeo) Zaccaria (died 1334) was the first husband of Guglielma Pallavicini (married 1327) and thus Margrave of Bodonitsa  in her right. He also carried the title Lord of Damala during his lifetime. As the elde
2 CONC st son of "King" Martin, born into the Genoese Zaccaria family which lorded it over Chios, Bartolomeo was a fitting match for the highborn Frankish heiress, who co-ruled with her mother, Maria dalle Carceri, and stepfather, Andrea
2 CONC  Cornaro. As a youth, he was forced to help raise a ransom for his captured father. During a Catalan invasion, Bartolomeo was captured and carted off to a Sicilian prison. Only by the beseeching of Pope John XXII was he released. 
2 CONC He was still young when he died, though he left a daughter named Marulla.
2 CONT ------
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#BenedettoIZaccariadied1307B
