2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT King András II & his first wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.         '''MÁRIA ([1204]-Trnovo Autumn 1237). ''' The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the first wife of "Alsannus rex" as "soror Bele regis Hungarie et…sancta Elizabeth" but does not name her[837].  Ephræmius
2 CONC  names "Maria de genus de populo Pæoanum" as the wife of "Asanes"[838].  Her father was forced to agree her marriage to effect his release from Bulgaria, where he had been captured on his return from Crusade in late 1218.  The His
2 CONC toria Salonitanorum of Thomas Archdeacon of Split records that András II King of Hungary was detained in Bulgaria by "Oxano Bulgarorum rege" until he agreed the marriage of "suam filiam"[839].  Her dowry included the cities of Beo
2 CONC grad and Braničevo[840].  She converted to Roman Catholicism[841].  Georgius Akropolites records the death of "Asano…uxorem Ungaram" at "citissime Trinobum" while her husband was besieging "Tzuruli castrum"[842].  m (Jan 1221) as 
2 CONC his second wife, IVAN ASEN II Tsar of the Bulgarians, son of IVAN ASEN I "Stari/the Old" or "Belgun/the Bulgar" Tsar of the Bulgarians & his [first or second wife] --- ([1190]-Jun 1241). 
2 CONT *2.         BÉLA (Nov 1206-3 May 1270). ... He succeeded his father in 1235 as BÉLA IV King of Hungary.  -        see below.    
2 CONT *3.         ELISABETH (Bratislava 1207-Marburg 10 Nov 1231, bur Marburg Elisabethenkirche). ... m (1221) LUDWIG IV "der Heilige" Landgraf of Thuringia, son of HERMANN I Landgraf of Thuringia, Pfalzgraf von Sachsen & his second wif
2 CONC e Sophie of Bavaria [Wittelsbach] (28 Oct 1200-Otranto 11 Sep 1227).
2 CONT *4.         KÁLMÁN (1208-killed in battle Sajó River 11 Apr 1241, bur Dominican church of St Mary Magdalene Čazma).  ... m (1214) SALOMEA of Poland, daughter of LESZKO I "Bialy/the White" Prince of Sandomir and Krakow & his wife G
2 CONC remislava Ingvarovna of Luck and Dorogobuz [Rurikid] ([1211/12]-10 Nov 1268).   
2 CONT *5.         ANDRÁS ([1210/12]-1234).  ... Betrothed ([27 Jan 1216/25 Jan 1217], contract broken 1219) to ZABEL of Armenia, daughter of LEO I King of Armenia [Rupenid] & his second wife Sibylle of Cyprus ([1216]-Ked 23 Jan 1252, bu
2 CONC r Trazarg).  ... m (1221) IELENA Mstislavna, daughter of MSTISLAV Mstislavich "Udaloi" ex-Prince of Novgorod, Prince of Galich & his wife --- of the Kumans. 
2 CONT ** She had two half-siblings
2 CONT *6.         IOLANDA ([1215]-Huesca 12 Oct 1251).  ... She was known as VIOLANT in Catalonia. ... m (Barcelona 8 Sep 1235) as his second wife, don JAIME I "el Conquistador" King of Aragon, Conde de Barcelona, son of don PEDRO II Ki
2 CONC ng of Aragon & his wife Marie de Montpellier (Montpellier 1 Feb 1208-Valencia 27 Jul 1276, bur Poblet, monastery of Nuestra Señora). 
2 CONT *7.         ISTVÁN (posthumously Swabia 1236-Venice 1271 shortly after 10 Apr).  ... m firstly (1263) as her second husband, ELISABETTA [Caterina] Traversari, widow of TOMASO de Foliano, legitimated daughter of PAOLO Traversari Pa
2 CONC trician of Ravenna & his mistress --- (-[1264], bur Ravenna St Vitalis).  ... m secondly TOMASINA Morosini, daughter of MICHELE Sbarra Morosini Patrician of Venice & his wife --- (-end 1300).
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT ===IVAN ASEN II===
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (Jan 1221) '''MARIA of Hungary''', daughter of ANDRÁS II King of Hungary & his first wife Gertrud von Andechs-Merano (early 1204-Trnovo Autumn 1237).  
2 CONT Tsar Ivan Asen II & his second wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         ELENA ([1224]-before 1254).  Georgius Akropolites records the betrothal of "imperator Ioannes…filium…Theodoro …undecim annos" and "Asanus…filiolam…Helenam…ab Ungara…novennem", a later passage recording their marriage at
2 CONC  "Lampsacum"[314].  Ephræmius records that "Lascari Theodoro" married "Asanis…filia… Helena"[315].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the daughter of "Alsannus rex" & his wife "soror Bele regis Hungarie" as the
2 CONC  wife of "Caloiohannes Vastachii filius" but does not name her[316].  Her father proposed her betrothal to Baudouin II Latin Emperor of Constantinople in 1228, but fearing Tsar Ivan Asen's ambitions, the Latins rejected the offer[
2 CONC 317].  Her marriage was agreed to confirm the alliance between her father and the Nikaian emperor, who were planning a joint attack on Constantinople[318].  m (Betrothed [1233], Lampsaka early 1235) THEODOROS Dukas Laskaris of Nik
2 CONC aia, son of IOANNES III Emperor of Nikaia & his first wife Eirene Dukaina Komnene Laskarina ([Dec 1221]-16 Aug 1258, bur Monastery of Sosandra).  He was crowned as co-emperor in [1241] by his father.  He succeeded his father in 12
2 CONC 54 as THEODOROS II Emperor of Nikaia. 
