2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rostislav_I_of_Kiev Wikipedia]  __ http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kievan_Rus%27#mediaviewer/File:Kingdom_of_Galicia_Volhynia_Rus%27_Ukraine_1245_1349.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT ( He or his family not really born or died in the Russian fereration etc. as marked many of the family-?) ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨
2 CONC ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨
2 CONT    http://faculty.utpa.edu/chebotkoa/main/ukraine/ukraine.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rostislav Mstislavich (Russian: Ростислав Мстиславич) (c. 1110 – 1167), Kniaz' (Prince) of Smolensk (1125–1160), Novgorod (1154) and Velikiy Kniaz (Grand Prince) of Kiev (1154, 1159–1167). He was the son of Mstislav I of Kiev and 
2 CONC Christina Ingesdotter of Sweden. After Yaroslav II of Kiev was driven out of Novgorod, Rostislav was invited to become the ruler of Novgorod. He accepted, and became the prince on April 17, 1154. Then, learning that Iziaslav II ha
2 CONC d died, Rostislav left Novgorod to take the Kievan throne. Indignant that their prince had abandoned them and angered that "he did not make order among them, but tore them more apart", the citizens of Novgorod drove out Rostislav'
2 CONC s son, David, who was their governor. They replaced him with Mstislav Yurievich, the son of Yury Dolgoruky. Rostislav ruled Kiev for one week before Iziaslav III of Kiev forced him to flee to Chernigov.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Possible disambigous:
2 CONT
