1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Yaroslav Glebovich''' (d. after 1199) - Prince of Ryazan, the youngest of the six sons of Gleb Rostislavich, the prince of Ryazan, from marriage with Euphrosyne (Evfrosinya), daughter of Rostislav Yuryevich, pri
2 CONC nce of Pereyaslavl.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Yaroslav Glebovich was first mentioned in 1187 in connection with an attempt by Bishop Porfiry of Chernigov to reconcile the Ryazan princes, sons of Gleb, with the Grand Duke of Vladimir Vsevolod the Big Nest:
2 CONT  ... the great men of Svyatoslavl, Yaroslavl, Vsevolodichev, and Olgav grandchildren, let him go to Ryazan with him, who were confiscated from Vsevolod. The bishop, having come to Ryazan to Igor and to Roman, Volodimer and Svyatos
2 CONC lav and Rostislav, and hiding all the men and ambassadors of the Grand Duke Vsevolozhy, and going to the prince in a different way twisting his speech, he was sent with nothing, not like a saint, but like a perpetrator and lies, a
2 CONC nd so you uttered evil speeches, and filled with swarming and dishonorable, leaving Chernigov in a different way.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1198, “Yaroslav, Prince of Ryazan, in agreement with the brothers, asked the Grand Duke Rurik and the Metropolitan to separate the Ryazan principality from the diocese of Chernigov and install a special bishop in Ryazan. And as
2 CONC  the grand prince decided, hegumen Arsenius was chosen and sent to Metropolite Joann. and this Metropolite placed him on the 26th day of September.”
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Gleb Rostislavich (d. 1178) - Prince of Ryazan (1145-1177 intermittently).
2 CONT Mother: Euphrosyne (Evfrosinya) Rostislavna (d. 1179) - daughter of Rostislav Yurievich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brothers and sisters:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Andrey? (d. before 1186) - mentioned only once before Roman Glebovich in the annalistic news of 1184, although Roman was a prince of Ryazan from 1178 to 1207.
2 CONT * Roman (d. 1216) - Grand Duke of Ryazan (1180-1207).
2 CONT * Igor (d. 1195) - specific prince of Ryazan.
2 CONT * Theodosia - married to Mstislav the Brave.
2 CONT * Vladimir (d. after 1186) - Prince of Pronsky (1180-before 1186).
2 CONT * Vsevolod (d. 1207) - Prince of Pronsky (until 1186, 1188-1207) and Kolomna (1186-1188).
2 CONT * Svyatoslav (d. after 1207) - specific pronsky prince.
2 CONT * Wife (since 1199): Vseslav - daughter of the Grand Duke of Kyiv Rurik Rostislavich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter:
2 CONT # Vseslava Yaroslavna.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#IaroslavGlebovichMVseslavaRiurikovna Medlands]
