1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander Glebovich (killed in 1223) - Prince of Dubrovitsky from the Izyaslavich Turov-Pinsky family. Son of Gleb Yurievich - Prince Dubrovitsky and Turovsky. Participated in the Battle of Kalka together with his 
2 CONC cousins Andrey Ivanovich Turovsky, Svyatoslav Yaroslavich Yanovitsky and Yuri Yaropolkovich Nesvizhsky. Together with Andrey and his son-in-law, he stood on the right fortified bank of the river, surrendered to the Mongols, and, t
2 CONC ogether with other princes and soldiers, was crushed when boards were placed on them, on which the Mongols sat down to feast.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Alexander Glebovich, the princes Svyatopolk-Chetvertinsky brought their family.
2 CONT
2 CONT He became Prince Dubrovitsky in 1190, when his father moved to reign in Turov.
