1 CONT
1 CONT Kublai Khan, Khubilai Khan or "the last of the Great Khans" (September 23, 1215 - February 18, 1294) (Mongolian: ??????? ????, Chinese: ???, also spelled as Kubilay Han in Turkic), was a Mongol military leader. He was Khagan (1260
1 CONC –1294) of the Mongol Empire as well as the founder and the first Emperor (1271–1294) of the Chinese Yuan Dynasty.
1 CONT
1 CONT Born the second son of Tolui and Sorghaghtani Beki and the grandson of Genghis Khan, he succeeded his brother Möngke in 1260. Kublai Khan's brother, Hulagu, conquered Persia and founded the Ilkhanate. Kublai also had a cousin name
1 CONC d Kaidu, who died in 1301.
1 CONT
1 CONT Contents [hide]
1 CONT 1 Early Years 
1 CONT 2 Mongol Empire 
1 CONT 3 Emperor of Yuan 
1 CONT 3.1 Invasions of Japan 
1 CONT 4 Dadu 
1 CONT 5 Later Life 
1 CONT 6 Notes 
