0 @N6000000002188003000@ NOTE Leo I of Halych
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Leo I of Halych (Ukrainian: ??? ?????????, Lev Danylovich), (born ca. 1228, died ca. 1301) was a son of King Danylo of Halych. Lev became in turn Knyaz of Belz (1245 - 1264), Knyaz of Peremyshl and Halych (1264 - 1269) and Knyaz o
1 CONC f Halych-Volhynia (1293 - 1301). He moved his father's capital from Halych to the newly-founded city of Lviv in modern Ukraine. This city is named after him.
0 @N6000000002188005102@ NOTE Svarn
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Grand Duchy of LithuaniaŠvarn the Lightning (Shvarno, Švarnas, Ioann) was the Knyaz of Halych, Grand Prince of Lithuania 1268 - 1269, Prince of Chelm 1264 - 1269. He died in 1269 and was buried in Chelm.
1 CONT
1 CONT His mother was Anna Mstislavna of Novgorod (died before 1252) and his father was Daniel of Halych (born 1201, died 1264) who served as Prince of Halych-Volynia 1211 - 1213 and 1229 - 1264 and Prince of Volynia 1215 - 1264 and was 
1 CONC crowned by a papal archbishop in Dorohychyn 1253 as the 1st King of Halych-Volynia. He married Mindowhowna, daughter of Mindaugas, in 1255.
1 CONT
1 CONT He had several brothers:
1 CONT
1 CONT Irakli Danylovich (1223 - 1240) 
1 CONT Lev Danylovich (1228 - 1301), Prince of Belz 1245 - 1264, Prince of Halych 1264 - 1269; he moved his capital from Halych to the newly-founded city of Lviv (Lwow, Lemberg) 
1 CONT Roman Danylovich (1230 - 1261), Prince of Black Ruthenia (Navahradak) 1255? - 1260?, and Slonim 
1 CONT Mstislav Danylovich (died after 1300), Prince of Lutsk 1265 - 1289, Prince of Volynia 1289 - aft 1300 
1 CONT He also had several sisters:
1 CONT
1 CONT Pereyaslava (died 12 April 1283, married Prince Ziemowit of Masovia in 1248) 
1 CONT Ustinia (married Prince Andrei II of Vladimir-Suzdal in 1250/1251) 
1 CONT Sofia Danylovna (married Graf Heinrich V von Schwarzburg-Blankenburg in 1259) 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT List of rulers of Halych and Volhynia 
1 CONT List of Belarusian rulers 
1 CONT List of Lithuanian rulers 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Vaisvilkas Grand Prince of Lithuania
1 CONT 1267-1269 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Traidenis 
0 @N6000000002188005086@ NOTE Roman Danylovich
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Roman Danylovich (b. ca 1230, d. ca 1261), Prince of Black Ruthenia (Navahradak) 1254 - 1258, Prince of Slonim?.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was born as a younger son of Danylo of Halych, a powerful prince of lands east from Cracow and later king of those regions, whatever it was called (Ruthenia, Halycia, Volynia).
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1252 he was married to Gertrude, Duchess of Austria as her third husband. He, in Western Europe, participated in her attempts to get the power in her duchy, under rivalling claimants. However, already next year they ended up in
1 CONC  divorce and Roman returned to Ruthenia where he was 1254-58 Prince of Navahradak.
1 CONT
1 CONT Contents [hide]
1 CONT 1 Mother 
1 CONT 2 Father 
1 CONT 3 Wives 
1 CONT 4 Brothers 
1 CONT 5 Sisters 
1 CONT 6 Daughter 
1 CONT 7 Sons 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Mother
1 CONT Anna Mstislavna of Novgorod, daughter of Mstislav the Bold (d. before 1252) 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Father
1 CONT Danylo (b. 1201, d. 1264), Prince of Galicia 1211 - 1213 and 1229 - 1264, Prince of Volynia 1215 - 1264, crowned by a papal archbishop in Dorohychyn 1253/1255 as the 1st King of Galicia 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Wives
1 CONT Gertrude, Duchess of Austria (b c 1223 - d. c 1288 or d. 24 April 1299), m. 27 June 1252 (div 1253) 
1 CONT Elena Glebovna of Volkovysk (b. after 1288), m. ca 1255 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Brothers
1 CONT Irakli Danylovich (b. ca 1223, d. by 1240) 
1 CONT Lev Danylovich (b. ca 1228, d. ca 1301), Prince of Belz 1245 - 1264, Prince of Halych 1264 - 1269, King of Galicia 1269 - 1301; he moved his capital from Halych to the newly-founded city of Lvov/Lwow (Lemberg) 
1 CONT Mstislav Danylovich (d. after 1300), Prince of Lutsk 1265 - 1289, Prince of Volynia 1289 - aft 1300 
1 CONT Švarn the Lightning (Shvarno, Švarnas, Ioann; d. 1269, bur. Chelm), King of Galicia, Grand Duke of Lithuania]] 1264 - 1267 (1268 - 1269?), Prince of Chelm 1264 - 1269 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Sisters
1 CONT Pereyaslava (d. 12 April 1283, m. ca 1248 Prince Ziemowit of Masovia 
1 CONT Ustinia, m. 1250/1251 Prince Andrei II of Vladimir-Suzdal 
1 CONT Sofia Danylovna, m. 1259 Graf Heinrich V von Schwarzburg-Blankenburg 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Daughter
1 CONT Maria Romanovna [1m.], m. NN, son of baron Stefan of Zagreb 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Sons
1 CONT Vasilko Romanovich (b. ca 1256, d. after 1282) [2m.], Prince of Slonim; he may (or may not) have been grandfather of Prince Daniel Ostrogski 
1 CONT Mikhail Romanovich [parentage uncertain], Prince of Druck; his alleged descendants include Princes Drucki-Lubecki, Drutskoy-Sokolinsky, Babichev, and Putyatin 
